            "advisory": "Affected versions of the keras package are vulnerable to Deserialization of Untrusted Data due to insufficient enforcement of safe deserialization rules for Lambda layers which allows invocation of internal functions. The keras.models.load_model path, even with safe_mode=True, permits a Lambda layer to reference approved internal modules such as keras.utils and call get_file with attacker-controlled arguments via the deserializer in keras/src/saving/serialization_lib.py, because the mitigation whitelists entire modules rather than specific safe callables. An unauthenticated attacker can supply a crafted .keras model and, when a user loads it, coerce keras.utils.get_file to download and write arbitrary files to attacker-chosen locations\u2014enabling Arbitrary File Overwrite and frequently Remote Code Execution (e.g., by overwriting ~/.ssh/authorized_keys).",
