            "advisory": "Affected versions of the Gradio package are vulnerable to Denial of Service (DoS) due to insufficient resource limits in the multipart parser. The `GradioMultiPartParser` class fails to enforce size limits on HTTP headers during multipart form data processing, allowing unbounded header accumulation. \r\n\r\nA remote attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending multipart requests with excessively large headers, causing memory exhaustion and denial of service. Additionally, the parser performed blocking file system operations using `os.stat()` during file upload processing, which could be exploited to cause performance degradation.\r\n\r\nThe vulnerability was fixed by implementing a maximum header size limit of 8KB (`max_header_size = 1024 * 8`) and removing the blocking `os.stat()` call in favour of tracking file sizes in memory during upload processing.",
